# netsurf: answer non-class setAttribute/removeAttribute marks locally
# when no stylesheet references the attribute (doc 20, stage 2 / T4)
#
# STATUS: SHELVED 2026-10-19/20 — implemented, builds clean, but NEVER
# gate-verified (two unsuccessful gate runs, below). Nothing from this
# patch is applied to the tree; it is not a regression risk to master.
#
# Design (doc 20 stage 2, first T4 kind by census order):
# A SETATTRIBUTE / REMOVEATTRIBUTE mark for attribute `name` on a
# BOX_BLOCK element is answered locally iff:
#  - `name` is not `id` (always declines — id selectors are ubiquitous),
#  - `name` is a presentational-hint attribute (21 names) or `href`,
#    i.e. its only rendering effect is the element's own box paint, and
#  - NO used stylesheet references `name`: html_rl_sheet_refs_attr scans
#    all sheets textually for `[name]` in any selector position, plus the
#    attribute-reading pseudo-classes (:link/:visited -> href,
#    :enabled/:disabled -> disabled, :checked -> checked/selected).
#    Backslash in a selector, an unreadable sheet, any doubt -> decline.
# Equivalence argument: with no sheet selecting on `name` and no hint
# effect beyond the element's own paint, style selection is unchanged and
# the box-tree delta is exactly the element's own paint state — what the
# full reconvert would have produced. Local answers are the same
# per-mark semantics as patch 301 (order, defer-and-retry, two-decline).
# Plumbing: attr_name rides the pending slot (+extras, freed in
# slot_drop; merge identity includes name); macos9_js_mark_dom_dirty_attr
# made public; try_local_one takes attr_name; 3 bridge call sites
# (macsurf_qjs.c) updated to pass it.
#
# Gate page (preserved alongside as staging/310-attr-local.html, prefix
# ATTRLCL): Phase A = 60 setAttribute on `data-x` (no sheet references
# it) -> answered locally; Phase B = 1 setAttribute on `data-flag`
# (a STATIC [data-flag] stylesheet rule) -> kind decline. The gate
# asserted the cumulative LIFE FULLCAUSE line:
#   total=2 over=0 nonode=0 kind=1 local=1 two=0 guard=0
# (the page's own innerHTML batch accounts for local=1).
# The adapted-script assertion (run-vita-sim-adapted.sh) was:
#   acl=$(awk '/page [0-9]*\\\\/[0-9]* NET-js-attr-local: navigate/ {on=1; next}
#   on && /page [0-9]*\\\\/[0-9]* [^ ]*: navigate/ {on=0}
#   on' "$R/netsurf.log" 2>/dev/null | grep -a 'LIFE FULLCAUSE' | tail -1)
#   case "$acl" in *"total=2 over=0 nonode=0 kind=1 local=1 two=0 guard=0"*) ;;
#   *) o2_bad="$o2_bad js-attr-local-census";; esac
# with a NET-js-attr-local line in the page list. Re-add both with the page.
#
# Gate runs (both disclosed):
#  1. FAILED: FULLCAUSE total=2 kind=0 local=1 two=1. Root cause was the
#     PAGE, not the engine: Phase B's stylesheet was appended dynamically
#     and the sheet was not registered when the scan ran. Fixed by moving
#     the [data-flag] rule into static HTML.
#  2. Never completed: stuck in the autotest phase >30 min, killed.
#     Undiagnosed whether 310-related or a host issue.
#
# Blocker (PRE-EXISTING, not a 310 bug — the 307 tree behaves the same):
# setAttribute marks recorded inside JS tasks (setTimeout callbacks) join
# the lingering load batch and never get fresh batch separation; the
# callback fires but the batch does not split. BATCHBURST (309) works only
# because its textContent marks happen to align with flush windows. When
# earlier batch marks decline first, the T4 kind census the ATTRLCL
# assertion needs is unreachable on this page shape.
#
# Resume conditions (any one):
#  - fix batch separation for marks recorded in JS tasks (batching
#    infrastructure; judged out of leg scope 2026-10-19), or
#  - find a page-driving pattern whose marks form fresh batches
#    (a synchronous post-load burst was NOT tried), or
#  - re-run on hardware, where flush pacing differs.
# Then: re-apply this diff onto the stage309 tree (it applies against
# upstream/netsurf paths), re-add the page + the adapted assertion, run
# focused ATTRLCL, then the full adapted gate.
#
# Diff below: work/applytest (310 tree) vs work/stage309 (309 tree),
# 2026-10-20. Debug instrumentation was removed before shelving.


